# ⚠ SECRETS FIRST — this is the important part.
#
# Docker does NOT respect .gitignore. Without these lines, `docker build .`
# from a developer's machine copies apps/worker/.env — DATABASE_URL and the
# service_role key — straight into an image layer, where it survives even if a
# later layer deletes the file, and gets pushed to a registry.
#
# CI never had the problem (the files are gitignored so they are not in a
# checkout); a local build absolutely would.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Build artefacts and dependency trees — rebuilt inside the image, and copying
# a Windows/macOS node_modules into a Linux image would break native binaries.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/build
**/coverage
.pnpm-store

# Not needed to build the worker.
.git
.github
.githooks
.claude
docs
correspondence
apps/console
infra
fixtures
**/*.md
!apps/worker/README.md

# Local tooling output
.drizzle-introspect
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
